[{:adr/next-steps-2011 "cloud-itonami-isic-2011 joins cloud-itonami-isic-8010, cloud-itonami-isic-5610, cloud-itonami-isic-8030, cloud-itonami-isic-2660 and cloud-itonami-isic-3812 as a sixth candidate available for a future :blueprint->:implemented promotion pass. '3510' (electric power) and '6120' (wireless telecommunications) remain flagged as candidates for a FUTURE pass, deferred pending careful redundancy-avoiding framing. The underlying :spec-tier pool remains far from exhausted (534 remaining 4-digit-class candidates plus 3-digit-group entries)", :adr/related ["2607101300-cloud-itonami-hazwaste-3812-blueprint" "2607100800-cloud-itonami-meddevice-2660-blueprint" "2607100300-cloud-itonami-missionops-9900-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9900 ADR-0001s (106 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607101400", :adr/west-registration-deliberately-not-done-2011 "same established precedent as every prior fresh-blueprint build this scope: none of the cloud-itonami-isic-* repos are registered as west projects. cloud-itonami-isic-2011 follows suit -- no :extra-projects/west.yml entry", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 5, :spec 535, :total 646}", :adr/manufacturing-lifecycle-framing-2011 "the Core Contract and Trust Controls text follows the SAME manufacturing-lifecycle framing ADR-2607100800 established (batch release as the governed 'real-world act' analog to a service vertical's own actuation op), adapted for chemical-process safety specifically (process-parameter changes and batch release without verification, rather than device-design changes and device-batch release)", :adr/candidate-screening-2011 "Several candidates investigated and set aside: '3510' (Electric power generation, transmission and distribution) DEFERRED -- cloud-itonami-isic-3512 ('Community Renewable Energy Operations', :implemented, :grid-policy-governor) already occupies adjacent territory within the same ISIC division 35, would need careful transmission/distribution-specific framing to avoid redundancy; '6120' (Wireless telecommunications activities) DEFERRED -- cloud-itonami-isic-6110 (wired network operations) and cloud-itonami-isic-6190 ('Community Telecommunications Access', :robotics true, requires :phone) already occupy the telecommunications niche closely enough that a mobile/cellular-carrier vertical would need careful spectrum-specific framing; '1200' (Manufacture of tobacco products) REJECTED on the same grounds as '2520' (weapons manufacturing, rejected at ADR-2607100600) -- dual-use/public-health-harm concerns disproportionate to this fleet's community-operator mission, regardless of it being a legal, regulated industry; '1101' (Distilling spirits) considered briefly, set aside in favor of '2011''s own richer, more universally-applicable regulatory grounding", :adr/blueprint-only-artifacts-2011 "published README.md, blueprint.edn, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, verbatim) -- SAME artifact set as every prior fresh-blueprint publication this scope. Deliberately NO src/test/deps.edn/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md", :adr/registry-field-replacement-2011 "the existing '2011' registry entry had its :repo, :business-id and :optional-technologies fields updated, and its explicit :maturity :spec override REMOVED so maturity/maturity-of now auto-derive :blueprint from the real :repo presence", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 106, :blueprint 6, :spec 534, :total 646}", :adr/blueprint-count-updated-again-2011 "ADR-2607101300's own (is (= 5 (:blueprint m))) assertion updated to (is (= 6 (:blueprint m))), continuing the 'not a fixed invariant' framing ADR-2607100500 established. Added a live-state corroboration assertion ((is (= :blueprint (industry/maturity \"2011\")))) alongside the five prior live-state corroboration tests and the synthetic-fixture-based unit test", :adr/date "2026-07-09", :adr/real-repo-naming-2011 "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2011 (public, matching every prior vertical's own visibility), following the SAME cloud-itonami-isic-#### convention as all 111 prior/sibling actors, rather than the legacy C####-prefixed placeholder scheme. business-id updated from 'cloud-itonami-C2011' to 'cloud-itonami-2011' to match", :adr/sixth-spec-authoring-build "SIXTH 'author a new blueprint from :spec tier' build, and the SECOND manufacturing-lifecycle pick (following the :spec :design :produce :inspect :package :audit shape established at ADR-2607100800)", :db/id -1, :adr/candidate-selection-2011 "'2011' (Manufacture of basic chemicals) selected: genuinely rich, well-known, internationally-distinct regulatory grounding (REACH in the EU, Japan's 化審法 Act on the Evaluation of Chemical Substances, US TSCA, Germany under REACH via BAuA), no redundancy with any existing blueprint (confirmed via grep across every blueprint.edn), clean robotics-premise fit (process-operation, sampling and inspection robots), none of the dual-use/harm-disproportionality concerns that ruled out weapons and tobacco. Legacy placeholder :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C2011) confirmed via direct GitHub API 404 check to never have actually existed. No bespoke capability library exists for chemical manufacturing specifically", :adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-2011 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword, :chemical-safety-governor, is grep-verified UNIQUE fleet-wide", :adr/test-status-2011 "kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 159 assertions, all green", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-2011 (community basic chemicals manufacturing) published as a fresh :blueprint", :adr/second-ethical-screening-precedent-2011 "establishes a second explicit ethical-screening precedent alongside weapons manufacturing (ADR-2607100600): tobacco manufacturing was also ruled out on the same dual-use/public-health-harm-disproportionality grounds"}]